# Authoritative source snapshots are verified by sha256 against
# examples/snap/sources/manifest.json. Git must never rewrite their line endings:
# with core.autocrlf=true a Windows checkout converts LF to CRLF, every recorded
# digest fails, and the provenance chain the project rests on silently breaks — in a
# way that depends on each contributor's git configuration rather than on the data.
examples/snap/sources/*.xml -text

# Golden fixtures and generated artifacts are compared byte for byte in tests.
examples/**/*.json text eol=lf
